    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.starter, mini.fuzzy?\n\n### Description\n\nCurrently, the mini.starter query only matches if you type verbatim the start of the link you want to select. I think that it's a decent idea to enable fuzzy finding for these entries (especially since the mini.fuzzy module exists).\r\n\r\nEx:\r\n- Help.md\r\n- **Hello_World.md** <-\r\n\r\n(mini.starter) Query: hewo\r\n",
